INT. FERRY GALLEY - DEPOSITION - NIGHT

A cramped steel galley converted into a deposition room. A long table, a court reporter's machine, a pitcher of water. Porthole windows reveal black sea. The ferry rocks gently, and the water in the pitcher slops.

ATTORNEY PRUDENCE KALINOWSKI-BAKER, 40s, sharp-featured, in a charcoal suit, sits at the head with a legal pad. Opposite, ATTORNEY THEODORIC MWANGI-FOX, 50s, rumpled, a pen behind each ear, flips pages. Between them, the WITNESS, HORATIO BLYTHE, 60s, a ship's purser in a stained uniform, sits with hands clasped. A court reporter's machine sits unattended, recording on its own.

A speakerphone in the center of the table crackles.

JUDGE OKAFOR-NIELSEN (V.O.)
(over speakerphone)
Counsel, state your appearances for the record.

PRUDENCE
Prudence Kalinowski-Baker for the plaintiff.

THEODORIC
Theodoric Mwangi-Fox for the defendant.

JUDGE OKAFOR-NIELSEN (V.O.)
(over speakerphone)
The witness is sworn?

HORATIO
I am, Your Honor.

JUDGE OKAFOR-NIELSEN (V.O.)
(over speakerphone)
Proceed.

PRUDENCE
Mr. Blythe, on the night of March ninth, where were you?

HORATIO
In the purser's office.

PRUDENCE
Alone?

HORATIO
No.

THEODORIC
Objection. Vague.

PRUDENCE
Who was with you?

THEODORIC ^
Objection. Compound.

The speakerphone hisses.

JUDGE OKAFOR-NIELSEN (V.O.)
(over speakerphone)
Counsel, one at a time.

PRUDENCE
Withdrawn. Mr. Blythe, who was in the office?

HORATIO
The first mate. Mr. Voss.

PRUDENCE
And what were you discussing?

HORATIO
The manifest.

THEODORIC
Objection. Calls for hearsay.

JUDGE OKAFOR-NIELSEN (V.O.)
(over speakerphone)
Overruled. It's a deposition.

The ferry lurches. The water in the pitcher sloshes. Horatio grips the table. Prudence waits it out, pen poised.

PRUDENCE
Mr. Blythe, did the manifest list the crates?

HORATIO
It did not.
